        "text": "In centralized exchanges, users deposit their fiat money or cryptocurrency to the exchange and trade within its internal systems users. Crypto is held in custody by the exchange, but it should be fairly easy to withdraw funds and keep them in your own wallet if you want to. The centralized exchanges operate as a middleman to facilitate the completion of transactions. The best centralized crypto exchanges provide a high level of security to users. For example, because cryptocurrencies are often stored in digital wallets, users can lose their money if they forget get their keys. A centralized exchange won't let this happen, as it safeguards the holdings on behalf of users. Moreover, centralized exchanges generally will ensure the safe completion of transactions. Because of this convenience and security, some users might prefer keeping their funds on centralized exchanges, particularly if they trade regularly or are new to crypto.",
